# Moneo Desktop

An Electron app that runs Moneo with its own private database on the owner's computer: no Docker,
Node.js, terminal or `.env`. The source setup (`npm run setup`, `npm run dev`) is unchanged.

## Build

```sh
node scripts/desktop/fetch-backend.mjs --platform win-x64   # native backend + mkcert → desktop/.build (see that script)
npm run desktop:build                    # Next.js standalone server + migrations → desktop/.build, main process → desktop/dist
npm run desktop:dev                      # run Electron on the unpacked build
npm run desktop:dist                     # installers → desktop/release (Windows NSIS, macOS dmg+zip, Linux AppImage+deb)
npm run desktop:smoke                    # drive the packaged app (desktop/release/*-unpacked) end to end
```

`desktop:build` runs `next build` with `MONEO_DESKTOP_BUILD=1` (standalone output in `.next-desktop/`, so
`.next` is untouched) and every `NEXT_PUBLIC_*` variable unset. It refuses to run when a `.env*` file
in the checkout sets `NEXT_PUBLIC_*` (Next.js would bake those addresses in), and fails if a local
Supabase address ends up in the output anyway.

Packages are unsigned by default. With `CSC_LINK` and `CSC_KEY_PASSWORD` set, electron-builder signs;
on macOS `APPLE_ID`, `APPLE_APP_SPECIFIC_PASSWORD` and `APPLE_TEAM_ID` also notarize. Unsigned macOS
builds get an ad-hoc signature. Package each platform on that platform (`npm run desktop:dist -- --win`,
`--mac`, `--linux`); the macOS and Linux backend needs a native addon built there.

## Where things live

- Package: `app.asar` holds only `dist/`, `setup/` and the icon. Next to it: `app/` (Next server),
  `migrations/`, `bootstrap/`, `backend/<os>-<arch>/`, `storage-api/`.
- Per user: the Electron user-data folder (`MONEO_DESKTOP_HOME` overrides it): `config.json` (backend
  secrets), `shell.json` (app port, tray notice, last backup), `postgres/`, `storage/`, `data/`
  (ChatGPT sign-in, bank certificate), `backups/`, `logs/`, `chromium/` (the window's own cookies).

The app listens on `http://localhost:47300` (chosen once, then kept: phone access, Scalable's return
address and ChatGPT's callback name it). If it is taken on the first run, a free port is saved instead.

## Behaviour

- Start: a small status window shows each step (the first run says it is creating a private database),
  then the app window opens Home. On failure it offers Try again, Open logs folder, Restore from backup, Quit.
- Closing the window keeps Moneo in the tray, so background syncs and phone access keep working.
  Quit (tray, Cmd+Q, `Moneo --quit`, OS shutdown) stops the server, then the database, then exits.
- Daily automatic backup while running; Back up now, Open backups folder and Restore from backup in the tray.
- Sign-ins (ChatGPT, banks, Scalable) open in the system browser and return to Moneo's loopback
  callbacks; the window reloads when it regains focus. Every other address also goes to the browser
  (https only). The window allows only the microphone and copying, for Moneo's own pages.

### Bank return certificate

Enable Banking returns to `https://localhost:3443`. On every start Moneo makes that certificate with the
bundled mkcert if it is missing (its signing authority lives in the user folder, `mkcert/`); nothing is
trusted yet. The first time the owner opens a bank's consent page, Moneo explains why and asks the
computer to trust that authority once: Windows shows its own confirmation (current user's store),
macOS asks for the login keychain password, Linux adds it to the browsers' NSS store (needs `certutil`).

## Security fuses

For a private copied-data preview, launch the desktop executable with `MONEO_DESKTOP_PREVIEW=1`.
This runtime-only flag prevents persisted Workflow recovery, the scheduler and the bank callback
listener from starting, and skips automatic bank/Scalable sync when opening a page. It does not
block network requests triggered by explicit actions in the app, and is
not an offline mode. Normal desktop launches and source development keep their usual behavior.

RunAsNode, `NODE_OPTIONS` and `--inspect` are off; cookie encryption, asar-only loading and embedded asar
integrity are on. The smoke test reads them back from the packaged executable. Because `--inspect` is off,
Playwright's `_electron.launch` cannot attach, so the smoke test drives the app over
`--remote-debugging-port` instead. DevTools are off in packaged builds unless `MONEO_DESKTOP_DEBUG=1`.

import { app, BrowserWindow, dialog, Notification, powerMonitor, shell } from "electron";
import { existsSync, mkdirSync } from "node:fs";
import path from "node:path";
import { backup, restore, startBackend, type BackendPaths, type RunningBackend } from "./backend";
import { createAppWindow, lockDownSession, openExternal, setAppPort } from "./app-window";
import { ensureBankCertificate } from "./certificate";
import { NextServer } from "./next-server";
import { backupsDir, home, log, readSettings, resources, setupHome, updateSettings } from "./paths";
import { choosePort } from "./port";
import { closeSetup, focusSetup, progress, registerSetupIpc, setSetupState, showSetup } from "./setup-window";
import { createTray, openedAtLogin, type TrayActions } from "./tray";

// MONEO_DESKTOP_DEBUG=1 allows debugging switches and the test hooks below (package smoke tests).
const debug = process.env.MONEO_DESKTOP_DEBUG === "1";
// A debugging port or inspector would let any program on this computer drive the owner's signed-in window.
const DEBUG_SWITCHES = ["remote-debugging-port", "remote-debugging-pipe", "inspect", "inspect-brk", "inspect-port", "inspect-brk-node", "inspect-publish-uid"];

setupHome();
const refused = app.isPackaged && !debug ? DEBUG_SWITCHES.filter(name => app.commandLine.hasSwitch(name)) : [];
if (refused.length) {
  log(`Refusing to start with --${refused.join(", --")} (debugging switches need MONEO_DESKTOP_DEBUG=1)`);
  app.exit(1);
} else if (!app.requestSingleInstanceLock() || process.argv.includes("--quit")) {
  // A second launch hands its arguments to the running Moneo; `--quit` with none running does nothing.
  app.quit();
} else main();

function main() {
  const paths: BackendPaths = { resources: resources(), home: home() };
  const hidden = openedAtLogin();
  let backend: RunningBackend | undefined;
  let server: NextServer | undefined;
  let window: BrowserWindow | undefined;
  let booting: Promise<void> | undefined;
  let busy = false; // stopping for a restore or a retry: service exits are expected
  let quitting = false;
  let failed = false;
  let port = 0;
  let backupTimer: NodeJS.Timeout | undefined;

  const message = (error: unknown) => error instanceof Error ? error.message : String(error);

  function fail(summary: string, error: unknown) {
    failed = true;
    log(`${summary}: ${message(error)}`);
    const [first, ...rest] = message(error).split("\n");
    setSetupState({ phase: "failed", error: { summary: `${summary}: ${first}`, detail: rest.join("\n") } });
    focusSetup();
  }

  async function stopServices() {
    clearInterval(backupTimer);
    await server?.stop().catch(error => log(`Stopping the server failed: ${message(error)}`));
    server = undefined;
    await backend?.stop().catch(error => log(`Stopping the backend failed: ${message(error)}`));
    backend = undefined;
  }

  function boot(reason: string) {
    booting ??= (async () => {
      log(`Starting services (${reason})`);
      failed = false;
      setSetupState({ phase: "starting", steps: [], error: undefined, firstRun: !existsSync(path.join(paths.home, "config.json")), version: app.getVersion() });
      if (!hidden || window) showSetup(!window?.isVisible());
      try {
        port = await choosePort();
        setAppPort(port);
        progress({ id: "certificate", label: "Preparing bank connections", state: "running" });
        const certificate = await ensureBankCertificate();
        progress({ id: "certificate", label: "Preparing bank connections", state: "done", detail: certificate ? undefined : "Unavailable; see the logs" });
        const running = await startBackend(paths, progress, { appUrl: `http://localhost:${port}`, appVersion: app.getVersion() });
        backend = running;
        running.onExit((service, code) => {
          if (quitting || busy || backend !== running) return;
          fail(`A Moneo service stopped (${service})`, new Error(`It exited with code ${code}. Try again, or open the logs folder.`));
        });
        progress({ id: "app", label: "Starting Moneo", state: "running" });
        server = new NextServer({ appDir: path.join(paths.resources, "app"), port, env: running.env }, error => fail("The Moneo server keeps stopping", error));
        await server.start();
        progress({ id: "app", label: "Starting Moneo", state: "done" });
        if (quitting) return;
        await showApp(!hidden || Boolean(window?.isVisible()));
        closeSetup();
        scheduleBackups();
      } catch (error) {
        progress({ id: "app", label: "Starting Moneo", state: "error" });
        await stopServices();
        fail("Moneo could not start", error);
      }
    })().finally(() => { booting = undefined; });
    return booting;
  }

  async function showApp(visible: boolean) {
    window ??= createAppWindow(port, {
      onClose: event => {
        if (quitting) return;
        // Closing keeps Moneo running in the tray: background jobs and phone access keep working.
        event.preventDefault();
        window?.hide();
        if (!readSettings().trayNoticeShown && Notification.isSupported()) {
          new Notification({ title: "Moneo is still running", body: "Background syncs and phone access keep working. Open Moneo or quit it from its icon in the tray." }).show();
          updateSettings({ trayNoticeShown: true });
        }
      },
      // Windows ends the session through the window; finish cleanly within the time it gives.
      onSessionEnd: () => void quit(),
    });
    // The server is up; a page that navigates on during this first load (a redirect, a click) is not a failed start.
    await window.loadURL(`http://localhost:${port}/`).catch(error => log(`First page load: ${message(error)}`));
    if (visible) window.show();
  }

  function openWindow() {
    if (window && !booting && !failed) {
      if (window.isMinimized()) window.restore();
      window.show();
      window.focus();
    } else focusSetup();
  }

  // Backups: one a day while Moneo runs, checked hourly so a sleeping computer catches up.
  function scheduleBackups() {
    const check = async () => {
      const last = Date.parse(readSettings().lastBackupAt ?? "");
      if (Number.isFinite(last) && Date.now() - last < 24 * 3_600_000) return;
      await backUp("daily", false);
    };
    clearInterval(backupTimer);
    backupTimer = setInterval(check, 3_600_000);
    void check();
  }

  async function backUp(reason: string, notify: boolean) {
    if (!backend) return null;
    try {
      const folder = await backup(paths, reason, { automatic: reason === "daily" });
      updateSettings({ lastBackupAt: new Date().toISOString() });
      log(`Backup (${reason}) written to ${folder}`);
      if (notify && Notification.isSupported()) new Notification({ title: "Moneo backed up", body: folder }).show();
      return folder;
    } catch (error) {
      log(`Backup (${reason}) failed: ${message(error)}`);
      if (notify) dialog.showErrorBox("Backup failed", message(error));
      return null;
    }
  }

  async function restoreBackup() {
    mkdirSync(backupsDir(), { recursive: true });
    const picked = await dialog.showOpenDialog({ title: "Restore Moneo from a backup", defaultPath: backupsDir(), properties: ["openDirectory"] });
    const folder = picked.filePaths[0];
    if (picked.canceled || !folder) return;
    const { response } = await dialog.showMessageBox({
      type: "warning", buttons: ["Restore", "Cancel"], defaultId: 1, cancelId: 1, title: "Restore from backup",
      message: `Restore Moneo from ${path.basename(folder)}?`,
      detail: "Your current data is replaced by this backup. Moneo backs up the current data first, so you can go back.",
    });
    if (response === 0) await restoreFrom(folder);
  }

  async function restoreFrom(folder: string) {
    busy = true;
    try {
      await booting;
      setSetupState({ phase: "restoring", steps: [], error: undefined });
      window?.hide();
      focusSetup();
      await stopServices();
      await restore(paths, folder);
      log(`Restored from ${folder}`);
    } catch (error) {
      busy = false;
      fail("Restoring the backup failed", error);
      return;
    }
    busy = false;
    await boot("restored");
  }

  async function retry() {
    busy = true;
    await stopServices();
    busy = false;
    await boot("retry");
  }

  // Explicit quit: stop the server, then the database, then exit. Forced after 20 seconds.
  let quitPromise: Promise<void> | undefined;
  function quit() {
    quitPromise ??= (async () => {
      quitting = true;
      log("Quitting");
      const notice = setTimeout(() => { setSetupState({ phase: "stopping", steps: [], error: undefined }); focusSetup(); }, 1_500);
      // A start in progress (the first one creates the database) is let finish, so nothing is left
      // half-started; the 20 seconds count from then.
      if (booting) await Promise.race([booting, new Promise(resolve => setTimeout(resolve, 180_000))]);
      const force = setTimeout(() => { log("Shutdown took too long; exiting"); app.exit(0); }, 20_000);
      await stopServices();
      clearTimeout(notice);
      clearTimeout(force);
      log("Stopped");
      app.exit(0);
    })();
    return quitPromise;
  }

  const trayActions: TrayActions = {
    open: openWindow,
    openInBrowser: () => { if (port) void openExternal(`http://localhost:${port}/`); },
    backUp: () => void backUp("manual", true),
    openBackups: () => { mkdirSync(backupsDir(), { recursive: true }); void shell.openPath(backupsDir()); },
    restore: () => void restoreBackup(),
    quit: () => void quit(),
  };

  app.on("second-instance", (_event, argv) => {
    const hook = argv.find(arg => arg.startsWith("--debug-action="))?.slice("--debug-action=".length);
    if (hook && debug) void runHook(hook);
    else if (argv.includes("--quit")) void quit();
    else openWindow();
  });

  // Test hooks (MONEO_DESKTOP_DEBUG=1 only): the tray menu's actions, and a restore without its dialogs.
  async function runHook(hook: string) {
    log(`Debug action ${hook}`);
    const [name, value] = hook.split(/=(.*)/s);
    if (name === "restore" && value) return restoreFrom(value);
    const action = trayActions[name as keyof typeof trayActions];
    if (action) action();
  }

  app.on("before-quit", event => { event.preventDefault(); void quit(); });
  app.on("window-all-closed", () => { /* keep running in the tray */ });
  app.on("activate", openWindow);

  app.whenReady().then(() => {
    log(`Moneo ${app.getVersion()} starting (home ${paths.home})`);
    lockDownSession();
    registerSetupIpc({ retry: () => void retry(), restore: restoreBackup, quit: () => void quit() });
    createTray(trayActions);
    // macOS and Linux announce shutdown here; delaying lets the database close cleanly.
    // (The event object is passed at runtime though Electron's types omit it.)
    powerMonitor.on("shutdown", (...args: unknown[]) => { (args[0] as Electron.Event | undefined)?.preventDefault(); void quit(); });
    void boot("launch");
  });
}
import { app, BrowserWindow, dialog, session, shell, type WebContents } from "electron";
import { appendFileSync } from "node:fs";
import path from "node:path";
import { trustBankCertificate } from "./certificate";
import { isAppUrl, isBankConsent, isExternalAllowed } from "./navigation";
import { log, readSettings, updateSettings } from "./paths";

export const devToolsAllowed = () => !app.isPackaged || process.env.MONEO_DESKTOP_DEBUG === "1";
export const iconPath = () => path.join(__dirname, "..", "icons", "icon.png");

let appPort = 0;
let reloadOnFocus = false;

/** Opens an address in the system browser. Tests log it to a file instead. */
export async function openExternal(url: string) {
  if (!isExternalAllowed(url, appPort)) { log("Blocked opening an address that is neither https nor Moneo"); return; }
  if (isBankConsent(url) && !readSettings().bankCertificateTrusted) await offerBankTrust();
  const testLog = process.env.MONEO_DESKTOP_OPEN_EXTERNAL_LOG;
  if (testLog) appendFileSync(testLog, `${url}\n`);
  else await shell.openExternal(url);
}

// The bank sends the owner back to https://localhost:3443; without this the browser warns there.
async function offerBankTrust() {
  if (process.env.MONEO_DESKTOP_OPEN_EXTERNAL_LOG) return;
  const { response } = await dialog.showMessageBox({
    type: "info", buttons: ["Continue", "Skip"], defaultId: 0, cancelId: 1, title: "Connect your bank",
    message: "Allow your bank to send you back to Moneo",
    detail: "After you approve access at your bank, it returns you to Moneo through a secure address on this computer. "
      + "Moneo made a certificate for that address that only this computer uses. Your computer will now ask once whether to trust it.",
  });
  if (response === 0 && await trustBankCertificate()) updateSettings({ bankCertificateTrusted: true });
}

/** Allows only the microphone (voice calls) and copying, and only for Moneo's own pages. */
export function lockDownSession() {
  const ours = (url: string | undefined) => Boolean(url && isAppUrl(url, appPort));
  session.defaultSession.setPermissionRequestHandler((_contents, permission, callback, details) => {
    const audioOnly = permission === "media" && "mediaTypes" in details && (details.mediaTypes ?? []).every(type => type === "audio");
    callback(ours(details.requestingUrl) && (audioOnly || permission === "clipboard-sanitized-write"));
  });
  session.defaultSession.setPermissionCheckHandler((_contents, permission, origin) =>
    ours(origin) && (permission === "media" || permission === "clipboard-sanitized-write"));
  app.on("web-contents-created", (_event, contents) => {
    contents.setWindowOpenHandler(({ url }) => { void openExternal(url); return { action: "deny" }; });
    contents.on("will-attach-webview", event => event.preventDefault());
  });
}

function guardNavigation(contents: WebContents) {
  const leave = (event: Electron.Event, url: string) => {
    if (isAppUrl(url, appPort)) return;
    event.preventDefault();
    // Sign-ins (ChatGPT, banks, Scalable) run in the system browser and come back to Moneo's loopback callbacks.
    reloadOnFocus = true;
    void openExternal(url);
  };
  contents.on("will-navigate", event => leave(event, event.url));
  contents.on("will-redirect", event => { if (event.isMainFrame) leave(event, event.url); });
}

export function createAppWindow(port: number, hooks: { onClose(event: Electron.Event): void; onSessionEnd(): void }) {
  appPort = port;
  const window = new BrowserWindow({
    width: 1280, height: 860, minWidth: 380, minHeight: 500, show: false, title: "Moneo", icon: iconPath(),
    backgroundColor: "#0f1011", autoHideMenuBar: true,
    webPreferences: { contextIsolation: true, sandbox: true, nodeIntegration: false, webSecurity: true, devTools: devToolsAllowed(), spellcheck: false },
  });
  guardNavigation(window.webContents);
  window.on("close", hooks.onClose);
  window.on("session-end", hooks.onSessionEnd);
  // Back from a sign-in in the browser: show what it changed.
  window.on("focus", () => {
    if (!reloadOnFocus) return;
    reloadOnFocus = false;
    window.webContents.reload();
  });
  return window;
}

export const setAppPort = (port: number) => { appPort = port; };
// Which addresses the app window may show, and which go to the system browser instead.
// Pure functions, so the rules are testable without Electron.

const LOOPBACK = new Set(["localhost", "127.0.0.1"]);

function parse(url: string) {
  try { return new URL(url); } catch { return null; }
}

/** Moneo's own server on this computer: the only pages the app window loads. */
export function isAppUrl(url: string, port: number) {
  const parsed = parse(url);
  return parsed?.protocol === "http:" && LOOPBACK.has(parsed.hostname) && parsed.port === String(port);
}

/** What may open in the system browser: https anywhere (sign-ins, banks), or Moneo itself. */
export function isExternalAllowed(url: string, port: number) {
  return parse(url)?.protocol === "https:" || isAppUrl(url, port);
}

/** Enable Banking's consent pages; the bank sends the browser back to https://localhost:3443. */
export function isBankConsent(url: string) {
  const host = parse(url)?.hostname ?? "";
  return host === "enablebanking.com" || host.endsWith(".enablebanking.com");
}
import { utilityProcess, type UtilityProcess } from "electron";
import { createWriteStream } from "node:fs";
import path from "node:path";
import { log, logsDir } from "./paths";

// Host variables the server needs to run on each OS. Nothing else from the shell's environment is
// passed on, so a developer's NEXT_PUBLIC_*, NODE_OPTIONS or .env-style variables never leak in.
const HOST_VARS = ["PATH", "Path", "PATHEXT", "SystemRoot", "SYSTEMROOT", "windir", "TEMP", "TMP", "TMPDIR", "HOME", "USERPROFILE", "APPDATA", "LOCALAPPDATA", "ProgramData", "LANG", "LC_ALL", "TZ"];

export type NextServerOptions = { appDir: string; port: number; env: Record<string, string> };

const READY_TIMEOUT = 90_000;

/** The Next.js standalone server in a utility process, restarted with backoff when it crashes. */
export class NextServer {
  private child?: UtilityProcess;
  private stopping = false;
  private restarts = 0;
  private restartTimer?: NodeJS.Timeout;
  private output = createWriteStream(path.join(logsDir(), "next.log"), { flags: "a" });
  private recent: string[] = [];

  constructor(private options: NextServerOptions, private onDown: (error: Error) => void) {}

  get url() { return `http://localhost:${this.options.port}`; }
  get pid() { return this.child?.pid; }

  async start() {
    this.stopping = false;
    const startedAt = Date.now();
    const child = this.spawn();
    await this.waitReady(child);
    child.once("exit", code => {
      if (this.stopping || this.child !== child) return;
      log(`Next server exited with ${code}`);
      // A server that ran for a while earns a fresh backoff.
      if (Date.now() - startedAt > 60_000) this.restarts = 0;
      this.scheduleRestart();
    });
  }

  private spawn() {
    const host = Object.fromEntries(HOST_VARS.flatMap(name => process.env[name] ? [[name, process.env[name]!]] : []));
    const env = {
      ...host,
      ...this.options.env,
      PORT: String(this.options.port),
      HOSTNAME: "127.0.0.1",
      NEXT_PUBLIC_APP_URL: `http://localhost:${this.options.port}`,
      MONEO_DESKTOP: "1",
      ...(process.env.MONEO_DESKTOP_PREVIEW === "1" ? { MONEO_DESKTOP_PREVIEW: "1" } : {}),
      NODE_ENV: "production",
      NEXT_TELEMETRY_DISABLED: "1",
    };
    const child = utilityProcess.fork(path.join(this.options.appDir, "server.js"), [], {
      cwd: this.options.appDir, env, stdio: "pipe", serviceName: "Moneo server",
    });
    const record = (chunk: Buffer) => {
      this.output.write(chunk);
      this.recent.push(...chunk.toString().split(/\r?\n/).filter(Boolean));
      this.recent.splice(0, Math.max(0, this.recent.length - 20));
    };
    child.stdout?.on("data", record);
    child.stderr?.on("data", record);
    child.once("spawn", () => log(`Next server process ${child.pid}`));
    this.child = child;
    log(`Next server starting on port ${this.options.port}`);
    return child;
  }

  private async waitReady(child: UtilityProcess) {
    let exited: number | null | undefined;
    child.once("exit", code => { exited = code; });
    const deadline = Date.now() + READY_TIMEOUT;
    while (Date.now() < deadline) {
      if (exited !== undefined) throw new Error(`The Moneo server stopped while starting (exit ${exited}).\n${this.recent.slice(-8).join("\n")}`);
      try {
        // The bearer header keeps the proxy from signing the owner in for every probe.
        const response = await fetch(`http://127.0.0.1:${this.options.port}/api/health`, { headers: { authorization: "Bearer readiness" }, signal: AbortSignal.timeout(5_000) });
        if (response.status < 500) { log("Next server is ready"); return; }
      } catch { /* not listening yet */ }
      await new Promise(resolve => setTimeout(resolve, 250));
    }
    child.kill();
    throw new Error(`The Moneo server did not answer within ${READY_TIMEOUT / 1000} seconds.\n${this.recent.slice(-8).join("\n")}`);
  }

  private scheduleRestart() {
    const delay = Math.min(30_000, 1_000 * 2 ** this.restarts++);
    log(`Restarting the Next server in ${delay} ms`);
    this.restartTimer = setTimeout(() => {
      this.start().catch(error => {
        log(`Next server restart failed: ${error instanceof Error ? error.message : error}`);
        if (this.restarts >= 6) this.onDown(error instanceof Error ? error : new Error(String(error)));
        else this.scheduleRestart();
      });
    }, delay);
  }

  async stop() {
    this.stopping = true;
    clearTimeout(this.restartTimer);
    const child = this.child;
    this.child = undefined;
    if (!child?.pid) return;
    await new Promise<void>(resolve => {
      const force = setTimeout(resolve, 10_000);
      child.once("exit", () => { clearTimeout(force); resolve(); });
      child.kill();
    });
    log("Next server stopped");
  }
}

